    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Supplementary Angles and Alternate Exterior Angles</strong></p>

<p>
Two angles are called <strong>supplementary</strong> if the sum of their measures is \(180^\circ\). 
When a transversal cuts parallel lines, we often see supplementary pairs 
(such as interior angles on the same side of the transversal).
</p>

<p>In the diagram above:</p>
<ul>
  <li>\(\angle BO_1Y\) and \(\angle YO_1A\) form a <strong>linear pair</strong>. Therefore, they are supplementary:  
  \(\angle BO_1Y + \angle YO_1A = 180^\circ\).</li>
  <li>Similarly, at the lower intersection, \(\angle CO_2X + \angle XO_2D = 180^\circ\).</li>
</ul>

<p>
This property helps us connect alternate and corresponding angles too:
</p>
<ol>
  <li>\(\angle BO_1Y = \angle AO_1O_2\) (vertically opposite).</li>
  <li>\(\angle AO_1O_2 = \angle CO_2X\) (corresponding angles when \(AB \parallel CD\)).</li>
  <li>Thus, \(\angle BO_1Y = \angle CO_2X\) (alternate exterior angles are equal).</li>
  <li>Also, both \(\angle BO_1Y\) and \(\angle YO_1A\) are supplementary since they form a straight line at \(O_1\).</li>
</ol>

<p><strong>Practice:</strong></p>
<p> Suppose \(\angle BO_1Y = {@angle_alt@}^\circ\). </p>
<ul>
  <li>What is the measure of its supplementary angle \(\angle YO_1A\)? [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</li>
  <li>
<p>Therefore what will be the measure of  \(\angle DO_2X \) and why?</p> 
<p> \(\angle DO_2X = \)  [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]] </p>
<p> Choose the correct justification for your answer above  [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>
  </li>
</ul>]]></text>
